                <pb facs="0847" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg759"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee instructs Mr. McCormick to ascertain whether the interested parties
                    will be permitted to present evidence before the council of admiralty on the
                    hearing of the appeal in case of the condemned portion of the cargo of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabia.</hi>)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
